== FS-66 phase 2B -- the two producer-dependent controls of the frozen checker ==
== plans/FS66-phase2-certificate.md §K.3, plants 9 and 12; §H Phase 2B's third item.
== 2026-09-21T04:48:21Z, the machine. Checker sha256 735b926798ffac14…
== Producer sha256 0a4bf94f089d83dd…
==
== These two need the PRODUCER, so --self-test (which runs plants 0-8, 10, 11 on a copy of a
== certifying file, standard library only) cannot contain them: they are documented MANUAL
== controls, and this file is their output.  Both are run on files written to a scratch
== directory, never into the repository -- a plant must not sit beside a certificate.

############################################################################
# PLANT 9 -- a certificate produced for the WRONG PROBLEM (c = 1).
#
# q(phi) = c*sum phi(1-phi) - sum_S phi phi.  c = 2 is the hand-proved constant (§S.2);
# c = 1 is a STRONGER constraint, so its B1 is smaller and its bound looks BETTER.
# The checker has no c to read: it rebuilds q from p with 2 hard-coded.
# MUST END: REFUSED IDENTITY_MISMATCH.
############################################################################

$ python3 tools/fs66_b1_cert_make.py 7 --c 1 --threads 4 --out <scratch>/plant9-c1-p7.json
*** CONTROL RUN, NOT A CERTIFICATE: c = 1.0, not the hand-proved 2: this file is for a DIFFERENT problem (plan §K.3 plant 9). The checker rebuilds q with 2 and must REFUSE it. ***
FLOAT READING (untrusted, double precision): value 14.000000 (dual 14.000000), status solved, 275 iterations, 0.2 s, 122.2 MB
*** the bound below is a CONTROL's, about a different object: c = 1.0, not the hand-proved 2: this file is for a DIFFERENT problem (plan §K.3 plant 9). The checker rebuilds q with 2 and must REFUSE it. ***
  U = 14002121709434441311357638455488 / 1000000000000000000000000000000 = 14.002121…
  (file sha256 003ae116dd1bd53514bbc7b2b75e1f3ee01fca8bee8c842b1e6c7966b633f3f1)

$ python3 tools/fs66_b1_cert_check.py <scratch>/plant9-c1-p7.json --m 3
REFUSED IDENTITY_MISMATCH: the two sides of the identity differ at 156 of 495 canonical monomials, the first by degree being y([0]): left -49000000000000000000000000000000, right -35859162227063000000000000000000, left - right = -13140837772937000000000000000000; y([0, 0]): left 0, right -12223175158887000000000000000000, left - right = 12223175158887000000000000000000; y([0, 1]): left 0, right 7341300912400000000000000000000, left - right = -7341300912400000000000000000000. Next: the producer recomputes the cascade, which by construction makes the identity exact.
  exit status 1   (1 = REFUSED, as designed)

--- the faithful twin of plant 9: the SAME producer, the SAME prime, c = 2.
$ python3 tools/fs66_b1_cert_check.py data/fs66/b1/cert-p7.json --m 3
