############################################################################
# PLANT 12 -- every weight vector replaced by ARBITRARY integers.
#
# The weights are the producer's choice of rounded cosines and sines, and they are chosen
# that way only because it makes U small.  Soundness never reads them (§C.3: E R E^T is
# positive semidefinite for positive definite R whatever the integers in the weight vector
# are -- the CONSTANT entry c included).  So replacing them must leave a file that still
# checks, with a larger and useless bound.
# MUST END: CERTIFIED or BOUND ONLY, never REFUSED.  A refusal here would mean the weights
# are on the trust surface, i.e. a design error.
# Registered prediction P-B4: U > 40 at p = 11.
############################################################################

$ python3 tools/fs66_b1_cert_make.py 11 --arbitrary-weights 20260921 --out <scratch>/plant12-arbw-p11.json
*** CONTROL RUN, NOT A CERTIFICATE: every weight vector replaced by arbitrary integers (seed 20260921) (plan §K.3 plant 12). The file must still check, with a larger and useless U: the weights are off the trust surface. ***
FLOAT READING (untrusted, double precision): value 28.201477 (dual 28.201476), status solved, 6275 iterations, 91.0 s, 745.0 MB
  U = 71566440172701215126555766209984785820692071348037 / 1000000000000000000000000000000 = 71566440172701215126.555766…
  (file sha256 eb7a298867a82731ec65220d7a4669bfb1a50da12dcb168465ff4ee0e1094dc5)

$ python3 tools/fs66_b1_cert_check.py <scratch>/plant12-arbw-p11.json --m 4
BOUND ONLY: every phi in [0,1]^121 with q(phi) >= 0 has sum(phi) <= U = 71566440172701215126.555766… (exactly U_num/scale of the file, sha256 eb7a298867a8…); but 4*U = 286265760690804860506.223064… >= 121, so this file does not refuse 4 colours -- which says nothing about whether 4 colours suffice.
  exit status 3   (3 = BOUND ONLY: a VALID certificate of a useless bound)

--- the faithful twin of plant 12: the SAME producer, the SAME prime, the cosine/sine weights.
$ python3 tools/fs66_b1_cert_check.py data/fs66/b1/cert-p11.json --m 4
CERTIFIED: every phi in [0,1]^121 with q(phi) >= 0 has sum(phi) <= U = 28.204320… (exactly U_num/scale of the file, sha256 683236677e0d…); 4*U = 112.817280… < 121, so BY THE HAND-PROVED LINKS L1, L2, L6 (data/fs66/b1/SOUNDNESS.md) no UD(Z/11^k, 2), k >= 1, is 4-colourable. Standard-library checker, NOT the Lean kernel.
  exit status 0   (0 = CERTIFIED)
  twin  sha256 683236677e0d55a4f9bd37d5266b370cebbb682831b3f0bc7493bce214bf0661
  plant sha256 eb7a298867a82731ec65220d7a4669bfb1a50da12dcb168465ff4ee0e1094dc5
  -> the digests differ, so the plant really applied.

############################################################################
# The colour-count controls on the PRODUCTION files (§K.3 plant 10's shape).
#
# The file proves a bound; whether it refuses m colours is the checker's arithmetic on the
# command line.  Every level of both towers IS colourable with one more colour than these
# files refuse, so a CERTIFIED here would be a false theorem.
# MUST END: BOUND ONLY, exit 3.
############################################################################

$ python3 tools/fs66_b1_cert_check.py data/fs66/b1/cert-p7.json --m 4
BOUND ONLY: every phi in [0,1]^49 with q(phi) >= 0 has sum(phi) <= U = 14.015224… (exactly U_num/scale of the file, sha256 f4b2ffa7c427…); but 4*U = 56.060898… >= 49, so this file does not refuse 4 colours -- which says nothing about whether 4 colours suffice.
  exit status 3

$ python3 tools/fs66_b1_cert_check.py data/fs66/b1/cert-p11.json --m 5
BOUND ONLY: every phi in [0,1]^121 with q(phi) >= 0 has sum(phi) <= U = 28.204320… (exactly U_num/scale of the file, sha256 683236677e0d…); but 5*U = 141.021600… >= 121, so this file does not refuse 5 colours -- which says nothing about whether 5 colours suffice.
  exit status 3

############################################################################
# What plant 12 found, recorded because a control that fires is worth more than one that passes.
############################################################################

This control is run in its STRONGEST form: every entry of every weight vector is replaced,
the CONSTANT entry c included, because §C.3's claim is about the whole vector.  Run that way
it went RED the first time, and the fault was the producer's: the linear form of a block was
written three ways (the all-ones block, a character block, a q block) instead of once, and the
character and q blocks' padded constant row R[0][0]*c^2 was omitted.  With the real cosine and
sine weights c = 0, so the omitted term is zero and the production certificates were never
affected -- which is exactly why only a control with c != 0 could see it.  The accumulation is
now ONE loop over blocks x weight vectors applying the three terms of (*) as §C.2 states them,
and the bug class is gone rather than the bug.  A weaker plant that had kept c would have
passed and taught nothing.

############################################################################
# The producer's own float controls at p = 7 (§H Phase 2B, first item).
#
# These read the RELAXATION, not a certificate: they say whether the thing being solved is
# the thing intended, before any rounding.  All three values are exact integers or halves,
# so a builder error would show immediately.
############################################################################

--- A. the quadratic constraint q dropped, the symmetrised edge cut kept.
    predicted 24.5 = n/2 (phi = 1/2 everywhere is feasible and the edge cut caps it there);
    this is the planner's control B2, plan §M.
FLOAT READING (untrusted, double precision): value 24.500000 (dual 24.500000), status solved, 100 iterations, 0.1 s, 121.0 MB

--- A'. q dropped and NOTHING else added -- the MINIMAL relaxation's own control.
    predicted 49 = n: phi = 1 everywhere is feasible for the moment blocks and the box rows,
    so in the minimal relaxation q is the ONLY thing that binds.  (B2 was measured with the
    edge-cut localiser present, which is why it read n/2 and this reads n.)
FLOAT READING (untrusted, double precision): value 49.000000 (dual 49.000000), status solved, 150 iterations, 0.1 s, 122.1 MB

--- B. phi^2 = phi added: the 0/1 problem, i.e. Lasserre level 2 for the independence number.
    predicted 14.0 = alpha(UD(F_7,2)).
FLOAT READING (untrusted, double precision): value 14.000000 (dual 14.000000), status solved, 275 iterations, 0.2 s, 122.8 MB

All three met exactly.  The bare minimal relaxation reads 14.014904, between the 14.0 of B
and the 49 of A': the 0.0149 is the gap between the second moment level and the integer
answer, and it is the whole reason U is 14.015 and not 14.
